BUILD_ONLY: ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:embodiedswe-<images/embodiedswe/VERSION> is never public (docs/protocol/README.md
§2.4, D5). Built locally only, not pushed anywhere yet; the EmbodiedSWE tasks name it in their FROM.

Why
  It contains NVIDIA Isaac Sim 5.1 / Omniverse Kit and the Isaac Lab 2.3.2 wheels (RoboLab's recipe, images/robolab/):
  NVIDIA licenses them for use, not for redistribution. EmbodiedSWE's asset bundle (Hugging Face
  EmbodiedSWE/robobench-assets) mixes licences, some non-commercial or store-licensed (CC BY-NC, Fab / Objaverse
  models): see the bundle's NOTICE / per-asset licence files under /opt/embodiedswe; redistributing the built image
  would redistribute those too. EmbodiedSWE's code is Apache-2.0 (LICENSE in /opt/embodiedswe).

What the builder accepts
  - the NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Omniverse licence agreement and NVIDIA's terms for the isaacsim / isaaclab wheels;
  - RoboLab's Apache-2.0 licence (its code and asset library come with the recipe);
  - EmbodiedSWE's Apache-2.0 licence and the licences of the assets in its bundle.
  No account, key or token is needed: everything is downloaded anonymously.

Inputs (all pinned)
  RoboLab's recipe verbatim (images/robolab/Dockerfile: its inputs are listed in images/robolab/BUILD_ONLY); pin 2.7.0,
  pin-pink 3.1.0, daqp 0.8.5, numpy 1.26.0, warp-lang 1.11.0 from pypi.org; EmbodiedSWE at commit
  67f44e8a2ca51c3e133867e5e669377778e8f97d (git, no history kept); its asset bundle at Hugging Face revision
  62fab5b70ccb0103c60c4ca39236abae2cc8e900, every file checked against robobench/assets_manifest.json (sha256) by
  robobench's own fetch_assets (the deformable suite's bundles excluded).

What the build changes in EmbodiedSWE (scrub_embodiedswe.py, in this folder; upstream is not edited)
  Keeps robobench/, LICENSE and pyproject.toml only; removes every suite's grader/ and smokes/ (the verifier ships the
  task's grader from its own tests/), the deformable suite and caches; strips all comments and non-module docstrings
  from the suites' binding files (configs/envs.py: calibration notes of solved bindings); rewrites the solve-calibrated
  comments and pointers in the shipped tasks' scene modules and text assets (stances, grasp cells and windows, release
  recipes, pointers to removed smokes and solutions; a `.usda` edit may touch only `#` lines); removes the working
  poses from two describe() texts (box_to_bin, wheel_carry: code confined to describe()) and
  robobench/scripts/robot_binding_smoke.py (a working reach driver). It checks that the code is unchanged otherwise
  (AST equality without docstrings) and that no banned phrase survives (`--check`).

Data
  None beyond the image: HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1; nothing is downloaded at run time. Frozen instances live in the task dirs.

Host
  As RoboLab's (an RTX-class NVIDIA GPU, NVIDIA Container Toolkit, driver 580.x checked). Unlike RoboLab, PhysX runs on the GPU
  (`device="cuda:0"`, as in EmbodiedSWE; embodied_first_exam/benchmarks/embodiedswe/rcb_embodiedswe.py).

Build (from the repository root)
  docker build -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:embodiedswe-$(cat images/embodiedswe/VERSION) images/embodiedswe
